    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20922" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hordĕācĕus</span></b>  (or
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ord-</span></b> ), a, um,
			adj.
		hordeum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>relating to barley</i>,
				<i>barley-</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">farina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 157, 5</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 20, 13, 51, § 135</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">panis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					18, 11, 26, § 103</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">farrago,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					11, 2, 99</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">messis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					18, 29, 71, § 295</span></i>
			: pira, <i>barley-pears</i>, i. e., <i>ripe at the barleyharvest</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 5,
				10, 18</span></i>.</div>
